# Credits

Third-party software and assets used by the studio's own code (constitution: "Bản quyền và nội dung").
Films record their own fonts, music and voices in films/<name>/CREDITS.
The desktop installers (specs/016) carry the parts below. Their license texts ship inside the core:
Python packages in each `*.dist-info/`, npm packages in `node_modules/*/`, Debian packages in
`/usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright`. `desktop/core-build/credits-check.py` checks this list on every release.

## Named parts

- Electron (https://www.electronjs.org), MIT License, the desktop app window (desktop/, specs/015).
- Desktop icons (desktop/assets/): drawn by desktop/assets/make_icons.py for this project.
- lemo-opuscar (https://github.com/lemomo-ai/lemo-opuscar), MIT License, the film library (lib/, pinned by library.lock).
- Python (https://www.python.org), PSF License 2.0. macOS: the python-build-standalone build
  (https://github.com/astral-sh/python-build-standalone), with the licenses of its bundled parts in `python/share/`.
- Node.js (https://nodejs.org), MIT License, with the licenses of its bundled parts in its LICENSE file.
- Chromium (full browser, for GPU rendering on Linux/WSL2, specs/019; Windows core and `sh bin/studio deps gpu`), downloaded by
  Playwright (https://playwright.dev), BSD-3-Clause and the licenses listed in its about:credits page
- Chromium headless shell, downloaded by Playwright (https://playwright.dev), BSD-3-Clause and the licenses listed
  in its own LICENSE files; renders the film pages.
- FFmpeg and FFprobe (https://ffmpeg.org), GPL-3.0, static builds. Linux: https://johnvansickle.com/ffmpeg/
  (source: https://ffmpeg.org/releases/). macOS: the ffmpeg-static and @ffprobe-installer npm packages
  (source: https://ffmpeg.org/releases/). The GPL text ships next to the binaries.
- Kokoro-82M voice model (https://huggingface.co/hexgrad/Kokoro-82M), Apache-2.0; downloaded at setup
  from the library's own release (onnx export by kokoro-onnx, MIT).
- Whisper models through faster-whisper (Systran/faster-whisper-base, base.en, small; https://huggingface.co/Systran),
  MIT License (OpenAI Whisper); downloaded at setup or on first use.
- espeak-ng (https://github.com/espeak-ng/espeak-ng), GPL-3.0, bundled by espeakng-loader for phonemes.
- Claude Code, bundled inside the claude-agent-sdk Python package, © Anthropic PBC, used under Anthropic's terms
  (https://www.anthropic.com/legal); each user signs in with their own Claude account.
- Debian packages of the Linux core (Windows): Ubuntu 24.04 (https://ubuntu.com) and the apt packages installed by
  deploy/core.Dockerfile (bubblewrap, socat, fonts-noto, fonts-dejavu, git, curl and their dependencies), each under
  the license in its `/usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright`.

